  <prompt>Port H6SolutionImportHandler.cs's 2 collaborators: (1) DeployDataverseSolutionsScriptImporter (Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1, 847 lines: pac solution import x3, pac solution list x2, pack/delete/auth) -&gt; Dataverse Web API ImportSolution / StageAndUpgrade actions with ImportJob polling -- the dependency-ordered 8-solution sequence (SpaarkeCore + webresources + 6 Tier-3 features, per this project's spec.md §11.1a authoritative count) ports as C# control flow, NOT a re-derivation of the ordering (the ordering is ALREADY correct and shipped in the pwsh script -- copy it); (2) PacCliSolutionVerifier (pac solution list --environment, PacCliSolutionVerifier.cs:113-116) -&gt; trivial Dataverse Web API GET /solutions?$select=uniquename,version. HARD PREREQUISITE (owed under every architecture option, not Option-D-specific): the 8 solution ZIPs must become VERSIONED PUBLISH/CONTENT ARTIFACTS the handler downloads/references, not files assumed present on a local shell's filesystem. Credential: the customer-env auth model per DS-4 (BFF app-reg secret sourced from H4-populated KV, per task 142's credential-config work -- NOT a new S2S secret).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse Web API ImportSolution/StageAndUpgrade async actions, ImportJob status polling, and packaging build artifacts for a code-based (non-shell) App Service runtime.</role>

  <goal>H6SolutionImportHandler.cs's import collaborator performs the SAME 8-solution dependency-ordered sequence Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 already implements, via Dataverse Web API ImportSolution/StageAndUpgrade + ImportJob polling instead of pac CLI. The verifier is a trivial Web API GET. The 8 solution ZIPs are packaged as versioned content/publish artifacts consumable by the code-based Worker site (no filesystem-shell dependency). order/retry/partial-failure outcomes are correctly classified; a parity test suite compares outcomes against recorded pac-based imports (DS-1b §6's heavy-port risk mitigation).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §2 (H6 row) confirms the credential gap explicitly: 'SolutionImport:ClientSecret KV wiring deferred (Program.cs:440-443) -- cannot authenticate even in-process (C3.10).' DS-1b §1 (H6 row) sizes this at 6-8 person-days and flags the SAME invariant as H2a's ARM-JSON dependency: 'Invariant under EVERY option: solution ZIPs must become versioned build artifacts in the runtime payload -- the fat container has this exact same problem.' DS-2b §1.2 corroborates H6 is the single LONGEST-RUNNING handler in the fleet (30-60 min), making it the dispatcher's lock-renewal sizing case (DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration=01:05:00 per task 102 is sized partly for H6).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/H6SolutionImportHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/DataverseWebApiSolutionImporter.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/DataverseWebApiSolutionVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md (§11.1a — 8 shipped solutions authoritative list)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H6 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="140" status="pending">H5 must have created the Dataverse environment this handler imports solutions into</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §11.1a">The 8-solution dependency order is ALREADY AUTHORITATIVE per Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1's $SolutionImportOrder -- port the ORDER verbatim, do not re-derive dependency ordering from solution metadata inspection.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-1b §1 H6 row">Solution ZIPs MUST become versioned publish/content artifacts -- this is owed under every architecture option, not merely Option D. Coordinate the packaging mechanism with task 116's blob-artifact pattern if a shared approach is more consistent than a separate one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-2b §1.2">This is the fleet's longest-running handler (30-60 min) -- ensure any retry/timeout logic respects the dispatcher's MaxHandlerDuration=01:05:00 sizing (task 102) rather than introducing an independent, shorter timeout that would fight the dispatcher's lock renewal.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H6 Web-API solution import port</topic>
    <files>
