    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, xhigh effort). Read Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 in FULL (847 lines) including its exact $SolutionImportOrder + retry semantics.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Artifact packaging">Package the 8 solution ZIPs as versioned publish/content artifacts consumable by the code-based Worker site -- decide + document the mechanism (embedded content vs blob-fetched, consistent with task 116/117's precedent where reasonable).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Importer">Author DataverseWebApiSolutionImporter: for each solution in the SAME dependency order, call ImportSolution or StageAndUpgrade as appropriate, poll ImportJob status to completion, apply the SAME retry/partial-failure semantics the script implements.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Verifier">Author DataverseWebApiSolutionVerifier: trivial GET /solutions?$select=uniquename,version.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Credential wiring">Wire the customer-env auth model per task 142's credential-config output (BFF app-reg secret from H4-populated KV) -- do NOT introduce a new S2S secret (this project's MUST NOT rule).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire up">Replace the 2 collaborators in H6's owning module with the new implementations.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Parity tests">order/retry/partial-failure tests + a parity comparison against recorded pac-based import outcomes (DS-1b §6's heavy-port mitigation for H3/H6).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'pac solution\|ProcessStartInfo' in the new files returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ImportJob polling under a live dev import shows a materially different completion-time distribution than the script's own timeout assumptions (e.g., StageAndUpgrade taking meaningfully longer via REST than pac's reported wall-clock), STOP and escalate to re-validate the DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration sizing (task 102) — a wrong assumption here risks the dispatcher's lock expiring mid-import, which is a correctness issue, not merely a performance one.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/DataverseWebApiSolutionImporter.cs</output>
