  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'pac solution\|ProcessStartInfo' in the new H6 collaborator files returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms the 8-solution import order EXACTLY matches Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1's $SolutionImportOrder (same sequence, same 8 solutions).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms ImportJob polling correctly detects success, failure, and a configurable partial-failure/retry condition.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms the 8 solution ZIPs are resolved from a versioned artifact source, not a local filesystem path assumed to exist on a shell.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The credential resolution path traces to H4-populated KV (task 142), with zero new S2S secret introduced (grep confirms no new client-secret app-registration reference).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 already implements the correct, shipped 8-solution dependency order and retry semantics; nothing to re-derive. Extension -- porting the proven ordering/retry logic to Web API calls, with artifact packaging (owed under every option per DS-1b) as the one genuinely new piece, is the minimal correct move. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H6 cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site, AND its credential is currently unprovisioned (Program.cs:440-443's deferred wiring) meaning it cannot authenticate even where it could otherwise run -- the entire Dataverse solution layer (H7/H10/H11/H12x depend on these solutions existing) stays permanently unreachable.</notes>

